## 4. Validation checklist

Run the commands inside the VMs. Save the output (or screenshots) for the README.

**Host checks (PowerShell):**

| # | Check | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| H1 | `Get-FileHash` of the ISO vs `SHA256SUMS` | Identical |
| H2 | `ipconfig /all` | **No adapter** in `10.10.10.0/24` (VMnet2 absent) |
| H3 | `ping 10.10.10.10` and `ping 10.10.10.20` | **100% loss**. The host cannot reach the lab. |

**Bastion checks:**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| B1 | `lsb_release -d` | `Ubuntu 24.04.x LTS` |
| B2 | `ip -br a` | One NIC with `10.10.10.10/24`, one NIC with a NAT address |
| B3 | `ip route` | **Exactly one** `default` route, via the NAT NIC |
| B4 | `ping -c 3 10.10.10.20` | 0% loss |
| B5 | `ss -tlnp` | **No listener on port 22** |
| B6 | `mokutil --sb-state` | `SecureBoot enabled` |
| B7 | `systemctl is-active ssh` | `inactive` or `unit not found` |

**Target checks:**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | `lsb_release -d` | `Ubuntu 24.04.x LTS` |
| T2 | `ip -br a` and `ip route` | Lab NIC `10.10.10.20/24`, single default route via NAT |
| T3 | `ping -c 3 10.10.10.10` | 0% loss |
| T4 | `lsblk -f` and `findmnt -rno TARGET \| grep -E '^/(var|tmp|home|boot)'` | Separate mounts for `/boot`, `/var`, `/var/log`, `/var/log/audit`, `/home`, `/tmp` |
| T5 | `sudo vgs` | `vg0` with about 3 GB `VFree` |
| T6 | `systemctl is-active ssh` | `active` |
| T7 | `mokutil --sb-state` | `SecureBoot enabled` |
| T8 | `sudo passwd -S root` | `root L ...` (locked) |

**Snapshots:** power both VMs off cleanly (`sudo poweroff`), then take a snapshot named `P1-clean-install` on each. Rollback is how we'll make Lynis before/after comparisons honest.

